{"availability":"available","full":"jimparis/qr-font","name":"qr-font","description":"A QR code generator in a TrueType font: https://qr.jim.sh/","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":520,"forks":15,"created":"2026-06-28T00:06:19Z","updated":"2026-06-28T00:23:15Z","license":null,"branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://qr.jim.sh/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T00:28:01.519Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T00:28:01.519Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T00:28:01.519Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:33:03.939Z","stars":520,"forks":15},{"at":"2026-10-08T00:28:01.519Z","stars":520,"forks":15}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This repo generates an experimental OpenType font that turns bracket-delimited text into a QR Code symbol while leaving surrounding text readable.","The fonts are generated rather than hand-authored. The build script emits glyph outlines and GSUB feature logic, then compiles them into dist/qrfont-.ttf. The default build compiles the delimiter parser, byte expansion, Reed-Solomon parity circuit, QR module placement, and fixed mask rendering.","Printable ASCII glyphs are copied from Liberation Sans Regular, scaled into the QR Font em square, so text outside bracketed QR blocks renders as ordinary text in the same font. Liberation is a reserved font name under the source font license, so the generated families are named QR Font 1-L, QR Font 2-L, and QR Font 3-L."],"features":["qrfont-1L.ttf (21x21 modules, up to 17 characters)","qrfont-2L.ttf (25x25 modules, up to 32 characters)","qrfont-3L.ttf (29x29 modules, up to 53 characters)","Printable ASCII input","Fixed mask pattern 0"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jimparis/qr-font/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"22d43d1e64000f422345a6aee23e0086e147b0f57f6ad6c1986d9cefa212e8c0","extractedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:04.030Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:33:04.030Z","projectInsights":{"ve